# WN22-SO-000300: Windows Server 2022 must be configured to prevent the storage of the LAN Manager hash of passwords.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: high
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-so-000300-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `critical`

    title `Windows Server 2022 must be configured to prevent the storage of the LAN Manager hash of passwords.`
    description `The LAN Manager hash uses a weak encryption algorithm and there are several tools available that use this hash to retrieve account passwords. This setting controls whether a LAN Manager hash of the password is stored in the SAM the next time the password is changed.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,high`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-53:IA-5(1)(D)`
    control_objective `WN22-SO-000300`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `1`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Network security: Do not store LAN Manager hash value on next password change to "Enabled".`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_IA_5_1_D `Windows Server implements IA-5(1)(D) by setting registry value 'NoLMHash' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Lsa' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Lsa`
        name `NoLMHash`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 1
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
